{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/pulls/2850","id":2968976711,"node_id":"PR_kwDOEFLz886w9v1H","html_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2850","diff_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2850.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/pull/2850.patch","issue_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/juanfont/headscale/issues/2850","number":2850,"state":"closed","locked":false,"title":"Filter exit node visibility through ACL policy","user":{"login":"Copilot","id":198982749,"node_id":"BOT_kgDOC9w8XQ","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/in/1143301?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot","html_url":"https://github.com/apps/copilot-swe-agent","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/Copilot/received_events","type":"Bot","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"body":"Exit nodes were visible to all peers regardless of ACL policy. This regression allowed nodes without `autogroup:internet:*` in their ACL destinations to see exit nodes in their peer list, differing from Tailscale SaaS behavior.\n\n**Root cause:**\nExit routes (0.0.0.0/0, ::/0) were unconditionally appended to `AllowedIPs` in `tailNode()`, bypassing the `policy.ReduceRoutes()` filtering applied to primary subnet routes.\n\n**Changes:**\n\n- **hscontrol/mapper/builder.go**: Extracted `buildRouteFilterFunc()` helper that filters both primary and exit routes through `policy.ReduceRoutes()`. Applied to `WithSelfNode()` and `buildTailPeers()`.\n\n- **hscontrol/mapper/tail.go**: Removed unconditional `node.ExitRoutes()` append since filtered routes now include exit routes when permitted.\n\n- **hscontrol/mapper/tail_test.go**: Updated test expectations to exclude exit routes when no policy grants access.\n\n- **integration/route_test.go**: Added `TestExitNodeVisibilityWithACL` verifying exit nodes are invisible without `autogroup:internet` ACL rule.\n\n**Example ACL requiring explicit exit node access:**\n```json\n{\n  \"acls\": [\n    {\"action\": \"accept\", \"src\": [\"mobile\"], \"dst\": [\"server:80\"]},\n    {\"action\": \"accept\", \"src\": [\"mobile\"], \"dst\": [\"autogroup:internet:*\"]}\n  ]\n}\n```\n\nWithout the second rule, `mobile` cannot see exit nodes despite them being advertised and approved.\n\n**Breaking change:** Networks expecting all nodes to see exit nodes must add `autogroup:internet:*` to appropriate ACL destination rules.\n\nFixes #2788\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT SUFFIX -->\n\n\n\n<details>\n\n<summary>Original prompt</summary>\n\n> Investigate https://github.com/juanfont/headscale/issues/2788\n\n\n</details>\n\n\n\n<!-- START COPILOT CODING AGENT TIPS -->\n---\n\n💬 We'd love your input! Share your thoughts on Copilot coding agent in our [2 minute survey](https://gh.io/copilot-coding-agent-survey).\n","created_at":"2025-11-01T08:27:52Z","updated_at":"2025-11-02T09:06:52Z","closed_at":"2025-11-02T09:06:52Z","merged_at":null,"merge_commit_sha":"5cf242ebb62cb233fdd7d9bce24243960402b500","assignees":[{"login":"kradalby","id":98431,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjk4NDMx","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/98431?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby","html_url":"https://github.com/kradalby","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/kradalby/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.gith